  "summary": "The TUI restart signal from the webui does nothing because the `on_restart` callback is never registered when ServerClient is instantiated in tui.py — the WebSocket handler in server_client.py (around line 403-409) receives the `restart_tui` message type and checks for an `on_restart` callback, but it's None since tui.py doesn't pass one during initialization (around line 2085). The fix requires: (1) wiring up the `on_restart` callback in tui.py's ServerClient instantiation to call the existing `action_restart()` logic (or a suitable variant that doesn't require a selected feature), and (2) the webui's restart confirmation and result feedback currently uses native JavaScript `confirm()` and `alert()` (in client.html lines 632-648 and index.html lines 1086-1102), but the codebase already has a well-established custom modal system (`.modal-overlay` with `.active` class toggling, dark themed dialogs) used for idea creation, script confirmation, rejection reasons, and move confirmations — the restart flow should be converted to use this existing modal pattern for UI consistency."
}
